## .NET build output
bin/
obj/
*.user

## IDE
.vs/
.vscode/

## Local secrets (contains a local XAMPP MySQL connection string / dev secret)
src/SASMS.Web/appsettings.Development.json

## Local HTTPS dev certificates (mkcert-generated, LAN-IP-specific, machine-local;
## never commit private key material)
src/SASMS.Web/dev-https-cert/

## Leave application supporting documents — uploaded files, not source, stored outside
## wwwroot (never web-servable) so they're never reachable by guessing a URL
src/SASMS.Web/App_Data/

## Docker Compose deployment secrets (MySQL app password, shared secrets) — real values
## live only in a local .env next to docker-compose.yml; .env.example is the committed
## template. Never commit the real file.
.env

## Real TLS certificates for the Nginx reverse proxy (see nginx/README.md) — nginx/certs/
## has its own .gitignore too, this is a repo-root-visible reminder of the same rule.
nginx/certs/*
!nginx/certs/.gitignore

## Python face-service virtual environment and bytecode cache — machine-local, rebuilt from
## face-service/requirements.txt
face-service/.venv/
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]

## Face-service runtime data — the trained recognizer model/labels and registered reference
## photos are real biometric data, never committed; models/*.task is the one-time-downloaded
## landmark model asset, not source (see face-service/README.md "Setup")
face-service/data/
face-service/models/*.task

## Local UI backup folders made during manual polish passes — not part of the application
ui-polish-backup-*/
